[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4337145249","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119021#issuecomment-4337145249","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119021","id":4337145249,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAoOVoQ","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-28T16:22:04Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T16:22:04Z","body":"I spent some time researching the MTL spec and found that this file format does not prescribe an encoding of RGB colours for `Kd` and other colour properties.\r\n\r\nMy suspicion is that it was common to write RGB values that were nonlinear sRGB-encoded to MLT files in the past, but there has been a trend to write linear-encoded RGB values in newer software. This is just a guess, mind you.\r\n\r\nWith this context, I don't think there is a clear-cut answer of \"this way is correct and this other way is incorrect\". Instead, as this PR states, different software interprets these values differently. I would argue that the way that the `Ks` property is applied to metalness would probably give a result that is closer to what the user would want if the RGB values are interpreted to be sRGB-encoded, so this PR is probably correct to not change those.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I think it would be better to maintain existing behaviour than to change behaviour. Having stable behaviour in an engine is overall a better user experience than having the engine behaviour change over time.\r\n\r\nIf we want to give an option to interpret MTL RGB as linear-encoded colour, we could provide an option in the MTL material importer. But I don't think this is worthwhile until we have more users reporting this bug and having real-world difficulties with the way that newer software is writing MTL files. There is also the challenge of how to interpret `Ks` and mapping it to metal: currently the importer interprets all RGB as sRGB-encoded values, including `Ks` and I'm not sure that the current hack  of taking the max of R, G, and B and mapping it to metalness would work well with linear-encoded values.\r\n\r\nAnyway. I think it's best to leave this as-is until we know that it's a big enough pain point for enough users to break compatibility with what is probably(?) the legacy way of encoding RGB values in MTL files.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4337145249/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4338229394","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119021#issuecomment-4338229394","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119021","id":4338229394,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABApQgkg","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-28T19:00:06Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T19:00:06Z","body":"I'd be interested in hearing from users as to what their software does. All I tested is that Godot mismatches Blender and macOS.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4338229394/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4339025229","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119021#issuecomment-4339025229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119021","id":4339025229,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAqBFTQ","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-28T21:00:34Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T21:00:34Z","body":"I expect a lot of software nowadays may encode colour using linear encoding, but the main sentiment than I mean to communicate is that it would be better to maintain existing behaviour, since this is likely the way that Godot has interpreted these files since Godot 3 or earlier(?)\r\n\r\nWhen users are authoring with Blender nowadays, they probably aren't using this file format, so the behaviour of modern software is likely less important than maintaining compatibility in this case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4339025229/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4339213363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119021#issuecomment-4339213363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119021","id":4339213363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAqMkMw","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-28T21:30:04Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T21:30:04Z","body":"I see the thumbs down reactions, but I'm uncertain about what you disagree with. Is it that I am mistaken that this is file format is not commonly used with modern software like Blender? I really don't know much about how common nowadays it is to use this format for defining a material colour and what software is commonly used to save the material file, so it's possible I'm mistaken on how often its used. If there aren't any existing bug reports, my guess is that it's not commonly used.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4339213363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4339848726","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119021#issuecomment-4339848726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119021","id":4339848726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAqzWFg","user":{"login":"Antiswitcher","id":30308663,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzA4NjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30308663?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher","html_url":"https://github.com/Antiswitcher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Antiswitcher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-28T23:36:18Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T23:36:18Z","body":"> When users are authoring with Blender nowadays, they probably aren't using this file format, \r\n\r\n> I see the thumbs down reactions, but I'm uncertain about what you disagree with. Is it that I am mistaken that this is file format is not commonly used with modern software like Blender?\r\n\r\n> [T]he behaviour of modern software is likely less important than maintaining compatibility in this case.\r\n\r\nCompatibility with what? Broken files that authors had to manually fix or find workarounds for? \r\n\r\nI don't think telling users of the software \"Sorry, that feature is permanently broken, you should know better\" is productive in any capacity. It should be fixed, and we should all move on to a brighter, better future.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4339848726/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4340390272","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119021#issuecomment-4340390272","issue_